Add live-lookup sweep + search to Available Services page (v0.138)

Dan's idea after finding out the dropdown-browsing approach doesn't
trigger any lookups at all: instead of relying on real orders of every
weight/destination trickling through over time to fill in the Available
Services cache, add a button that proactively sweeps a fixed spread of
representative postcodes at a light nominal weight, so the different
service tiers each UK delivery zone offers get pulled in in one go.

Backend (DpdShippingService/ApcShippingService):
- Extracted the Order-dependent parts of the live lookup (postcode,
  country, weight, parcel/piece count, and for APC the goods value too)
  out into a plain-values "Raw" variant of the existing body builder, so
  it can be called with a probe postcode instead of a real order, while
  the real order-driven lookup (listAvailableServices/
  checkServiceAvailability) now just works out those values and calls the
  same Raw method - no behaviour change there.
- ApcShippingService.postWithDimensionRetry() changed from taking a
  Function<Order, ObjectNode> + Order to a plain Supplier<ObjectNode>, so
  it no longer needs an Order at all - every call site now passes a
  lambda capturing whatever it actually needs.
- New SERVICE_SWEEP_POSTCODES (one list per courier, same 8 postcodes):
  BNS's own WN6 0XF, Northern Ireland (BT1 1AA), Scottish Highlands
  (IV1 1AA), a Scottish island/Orkney (KW15 1AA), the Channel Islands/
  Jersey (JE1 1AA), Isle of Man (IM1 1AA), Isle of Wight (PO30 1AA), and
  the Isles of Scilly (TR21 0AA) - all sent with country code GB, since
  none of these are a separate sovereign country for postal purposes.
- New refreshAllKnownServices() on both services: runs the live lookup
  once per sweep postcode at 0.5kg (APC: 1 piece, nominal £10 goods
  value), merging each result into the existing last-known-services cache
  (the merge logic from v0.136, unchanged) rather than replacing it. One
  postcode's call failing doesn't abort the sweep - its postcode and
  error are collected into a warnings list instead, returned to the
  frontend rather than silently swallowed.
- New AvailableServicesRefreshResult DTO (services + warnings), and new
  POST /settings/dpd/available-services/refresh and
  POST /settings/apc/available-services/refresh endpoints on
  SettingsController.

Frontend:
- AvailableServices.tsx: "Refresh from live lookup" button calling the
  new refresh endpoint, re-populating the page's own tick state from the
  result and showing any warnings inline; a search bar filtering by
  service name or code, since the list can now be considerably longer.

